Zed Preview now supports custom ollama token limits via settings.json.  Out of the box you should see `llama3.1:latest` will now use 16384, but you can tweak this to match your hardware's capabilities.   

```json
{
  "language_models": {
    "ollama": {
      "available_models": [
        {
          "provider": "ollama",
          "name": "llama3.1:latest",
          "max_tokens": 65536
        }
      ]
    }
  }
}
```

I've also updated the [Zed Ollama Configuration Docs](https://zed.dev/docs/assistant/configuration#ollama-context).  Thanks for reporting!

